{#
_row_menus.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The snooze and spam menus of the list rows: one of each for the whole list,
opened for whichever row's button was pressed (#496).

Every row used to carry its own copy of both. Nobody opens fifty menus, and
fifty copies were a third of each row's markup and three of its four Stimulus
controllers — built, connected and refreshed on every folder change and every
category tab, which is what made switching between them slow. The rows keep
their buttons; the buttons point here with aria-controls, and mail--row-menus
fills, places and opens the menu for the row that asked.

Outside the list frame, so it is drawn once per page and not again on every
list navigation, and so a refresh of the list never morphs a menu that is open.
Placed in the top layer when it opens (see mail--row-menus#place), so the
blurred panes around the list cannot clip or trap it.
#}
<div data-controller="mail--row-menus"
     data-action="mail:row-menu@document->mail--row-menus#open">

    {% include '_partials/_snooze_menu.html.twig' with {
        controller: 'mail--row-menus',
        method:     'snooze',
        shared:     true,
    } only %}

    {# The spam menu, as a list row's button would have drawn it: its panel is
       empty here and filled from the row's own URL when it opens. No trigger of
       its own — the row's button is the anchor, handed over in openFor(). #}
    <div data-controller="mail--spam-menu"
         data-mail--row-menus-target="spam"
         data-mail--spam-menu-closes-pane-value="false"
         data-mail--spam-menu-align-value="end">
        <div id="row-spam-menu"
             data-mail--spam-menu-target="panel"
             data-action="click->mail--spam-menu#stop"
             role="menu"
             aria-label="{{ 'toolbar.actions.spam'|trans }}"
             class="hidden visible absolute right-0 top-full mt-1 z-30 w-80 max-h-96 overflow-y-auto rounded-pane
                    bg-pane-soft backdrop-blur-sm
                    border border-line
                    shadow-pop py-1 text-left"></div>
    </div>
</div>
